From a72a364bd6fd1673ab56a81653d46bb3697be202 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: satoshinotdead <dev@criptonautas.co>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 23:05:36 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] FEATURE: anonist hops right of the header search, themed
 hoodie and a salute on click

---
 AGENTS.md                                     |   6 +-
 README.es.md                                  |   4 +-
 README.md                                     |   4 +-
 common/common.scss                            |  48 +++++++-
 docs/anonist-sprite.svg                       |  21 ++--
 docs/frames.png                               | Bin 21695 -> 23466 bytes
 docs/frames.py                                |  34 ++++--
 .../discourse/components/nautas-mascot.gjs    |  14 ++-
 javascripts/discourse/lib/mascot-frames.js    | 115 ++++++++++++++++--
 test/acceptance/nautas-mascot-test.js         |  11 +-
 10 files changed, 219 insertions(+), 38 deletions(-)

diff --git a/AGENTS.md b/AGENTS.md
index 7c01546..0f1b58d 100644
--- a/AGENTS.md
+++ b/AGENTS.md
@@ -19,7 +19,7 @@ docs/                                          ← frame sheet and sprite (art s
 
 - Frames are pixel art on a 48×48 grid, drawn in `docs/frames.py`. Never edit `mascot-frames.js`, the sprite or `frames.png` by hand; run `python3 docs/frames.py` (the sheet needs Pillow).
 - Motion is in steps only (`steps(1, end)`), never eased tweens, and nothing flashes. Keep the `prefers-reduced-motion` block in sync with any new animation.
-- State is classes on the `.nautas-mascot` element (`--look`, `--nod`, `--think`, `--wink`), set from DOM events. The search menu marks a running search with `.loading` on `.search-menu-container`; that is the only signal read from core.
+- State is classes on the `.nautas-mascot` element (`--look`, `--nod`, `--think`, `--wink`, the `--walk`/`--hop` routines and the `--salute` easter egg on click), set from DOM events. The search menu marks a running search with `.loading` on `.search-menu-container`; that is the only signal read from core.
 - The mascot is decorative: `aria-hidden`, no text of its own.
 - BEM class names, `--d-*`/core color variables over hardcoded colors (the mask colors are the brand's and stay fixed).
 - Templates use `{{}}` only; no `innerHTML`.
@@ -37,6 +37,8 @@ Add conventions and gotchas you discover to this file, in the same PR.
 - In `.gjs` templates a block param named like an HTML/SVG tag turns that tag into a component call: `{{#each paths as |path|}}<path />` crashes the whole search menu. Never name block params after tags.
 - QUnit does not load theme CSS, so `isVisible()` is meaningless there; assert the `hidden` attribute instead. On `/` only the welcome-banner search exists; the header field appears once the banner scrolls away.
 - System specs run with `Capybara.disable_animation`, so any frame shown only by a keyframe disappears in screenshots; the idle frame keeps `opacity: 1` at rest. On Horizon's `/` the search is the welcome-banner one.
-- anonist stands outside the field: on the top border in the welcome banner, left of it in the header. Horizon's header is 52 px, which fits the 48 px figure plus its 4 px hop; check it there after any size change.
+- anonist stands outside the field: on the top border in the welcome banner; right of it in the header, mirrored to face the field, over a floor drawn by the host's `::after` (the mascot itself moves). Horizon's header is 52 px, which fits the 48 px figure plus its 4 px hop; check it there after any size change.
+- The hoodie pixels carry `nautas-mascot__hood`/`__hood-shade` classes (from `CLASSES` in `docs/frames.py`); CSS recolors them with `--primary-medium`, the `fill` is only the sprite's fallback.
+- The salute click is stopped from propagating, so it doesn't open the search menu; it stays an easter egg (no pointer cursor, still `aria-hidden`).
 - Walk and hop durations live in both `common.scss` (`$walk-step`, `$hop-step`) and `MOVES` in the component; change them together.
 - To run CI locally: the `discourse/discourse_test:slim-browsers` image (what [dv](https://github.com/discourse/dv) builds on) with the steps of `discourse/.github`'s `discourse-theme.yml`; set `CI=1` so Chrome starts with `--no-sandbox`.
diff --git a/README.es.md b/README.es.md
index e97500b..cb32ca4 100644
--- a/README.es.md
+++ b/README.es.md
@@ -12,13 +12,13 @@ Componente de tema para Discourse que pone a **anonist**, la mascota de la comun
 
 ## Qué hace
 
-anonist se para junto al buscador, por fuera, y se mueve en pasos, estilo 8 bits. El buscador conserva su lupa.
+anonist se para junto al buscador, por fuera, y se mueve en pasos, estilo 8 bits. El buscador conserva su lupa. Su buzo toma el tono medio del tema, así encaja en esquemas claros y oscuros.
 
 | Cuándo | Cuadro |
 |---|---|
 | No pasa nada | respira (sube un píxel) y pestañea cada tanto |
 | Al cargar y cada ~20 s, banner de bienvenida | camina sobre el borde superior del buscador y vuelve |
-| Al cargar y cada ~20 s, encabezado | salta tres pasos a la derecha, tres de vuelta y mira el buscador |
+| Al cargar y cada ~20 s, encabezado | se para a la derecha del buscador sobre un piso tenue, salta tres pasos a la derecha, tres de vuelta y mira el buscador |
 | El buscador recibe foco | mira lo que escribes |
 | Haces una pausa al escribir | asiente un píxel |
 | La búsqueda está corriendo | piensa, con tres puntos que se encienden |
diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index d84aa63..51ebf41 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -12,13 +12,13 @@ A Discourse theme component that puts **anonist**, the community mascot, in the
 
 ## What it does
 
-anonist stands next to the field, outside it, and moves in steps, 8-bit style. The field keeps its magnifier.
+anonist stands next to the field, outside it, and moves in steps, 8-bit style. The field keeps its magnifier. His hoodie takes the theme's mid tone, so it fits light and dark color schemes.
 
 | When | Frame |
 |---|---|
 | Nothing happens | breathes (up one pixel) and blinks now and then |
 | On load and every ~20 s, welcome banner | walks along the field's top border and back |
-| On load and every ~20 s, header | hops three steps right, three back, then looks at the field |
+| On load and every ~20 s, header | stands right of the field on a faint floor, hops three steps right, three back, then looks at the field |
 | The field gets focus | looks at what you type |
 | You pause while typing | nods one pixel |
 | The search is running | thinks, with three dots lighting up |
diff --git a/common/common.scss b/common/common.scss
index 8b3398a..94c2ad9 100644
--- a/common/common.scss
+++ b/common/common.scss
@@ -10,6 +10,18 @@ $hop-step: 0.13s;
   position: relative;
 }
 
+// header: a faint floor right of the field, under the hops (static, unlike the mascot)
+.search-input--header.nautas-mascot-host::after {
+  content: "";
+  position: absolute;
+  inset-block-start: calc(50% + #{$px} * 25);
+  inset-inline-start: calc(100% + #{$px} * 2);
+  inline-size: calc(#{$px} * 60);
+  block-size: calc(#{$px} * 2);
+  background: var(--primary-low);
+  pointer-events: none;
+}
+
 .nautas-mascot {
   position: absolute;
   inline-size: $size;
@@ -27,11 +39,11 @@ $hop-step: 0.13s;
     inset-inline-start: 0.4em;
   }
 
-  // header: left of the field, centred on it and 2 px low, so the 4 px hops stay inside
-  // the bar; 3 hops (24 px) reach the field's border
+  // header: right of the field, facing it, on the floor; centred on the field and 2 px low,
+  // so the 4 px hops stay inside the bar
   .search-input--header & {
     inset-block-start: calc(50% - #{$size} / 2 + #{$px} * 2);
-    inset-inline-end: calc(100% + #{$px} * 16);
+    inset-inline-start: calc(100% - #{$px} * 4);
   }
 
   &__art {
@@ -39,6 +51,21 @@ $hop-step: 0.13s;
     inline-size: 100%;
     block-size: 100%;
     overflow: visible;
+    pointer-events: auto; // for the salute
+  }
+
+  // facing the field; the salute keeps his right hand
+  .search-input--header &:not(.nautas-mascot--salute) .nautas-mascot__art {
+    scale: -1 1;
+  }
+
+  // the hoodie follows the theme: a mid tone on light and dark schemes alike
+  &__hood {
+    fill: var(--primary-medium);
+  }
+
+  &__hood-shade {
+    fill: color-mix(in srgb, var(--primary-medium) 82%, #000);
   }
 
   &__frame {
@@ -117,6 +144,21 @@ $hop-step: 0.13s;
     }
   }
 
+  // easter egg: salutes when clicked
+  &--salute {
+    animation: none;
+
+    .nautas-mascot__frame,
+    .nautas-mascot__dot {
+      animation: none;
+      opacity: 0;
+    }
+
+    .nautas-mascot__frame--salute {
+      opacity: 1;
+    }
+  }
+
   // routines: walk in place (welcome banner), hop right and back (header)
   &--walk,
   &--hop {
